            "type": "paragraph",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "At a Year 12 formal, 45% of the students travelled to the event in a hired limousine, while the remaining 55% were driven to the event by a parent."
              }
            ],
            "spaceAfter": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "p42-q27-stem-2",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Of the students who travelled in a hired limousine, 30% had a professional photo taken."
              }
            ],
            "spaceAfter": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "p42-q27-stem-3",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Of the students who were driven by a parent, 60% had a professional photo taken."
              }
            ],
            "spaceAfter": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "p42-q27-stem-4",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Given that a student had a professional photo taken, what is the probability that the student travelled to the event in a hired limousine?"
              }
            ],
            "spaceAfter": 1
          }
        ]
      },
      "answerSpaceMm": 52,
      "answer": {
        "short": "$\\dfrac{9}{31}$",
        "worked": "Let $L$ denote travel in a hired limousine and $F$ denote having a professional photo taken. The tree uses travel method first, followed by whether a photo was taken.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(L\\cap F)&=0.45\\times0.30\\\\&=0.135\\\\P(F)&=0.45\\times0.30+0.55\\times0.60\\\\&=0.465\\\\P(L\\mid F)&=\\frac{P(L\\cap F)}{P(F)}\\\\&=\\frac{0.45\\times0.30}{(0.45\\times0.30)+(0.55\\times0.60)}\\\\&=\\frac{9}{31}\\end{align*}$$",
        "provenance": {
          "short": "source",
          "worked": "authored"
        },
